From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:41:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] droidbufferpool: do not leak the allocator of each
 configuration

set_config() made a new allocator for the pool and took a second
reference to it with gst_object_ref(). A new allocator is a GstObject
with a floating reference, so it then had two, and finalize let go of
only one: every pool configuration leaked an allocator. A pool that is
configured again also overwrote the allocator of its last configuration
without letting go of it.

Sink the new allocator's floating reference instead, and let go of the
earlier one when the pool is configured again; memory made by it holds a
reference of its own.

Found with LeakSanitizer, by the buffer pool unit tests.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/sailfishos/gst-droid/pull/91]
---
 gst-libs/gst/droid/gstdroidbufferpool.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gst-libs/gst/droid/gstdroidbufferpool.c b/gst-libs/gst/droid/gstdroidbufferpool.c
index c66761c..97fa90b 100644
--- a/gst-libs/gst/droid/gstdroidbufferpool.c
+++ b/gst-libs/gst/droid/gstdroidbufferpool.c
@@ -63,8 +63,11 @@ gst_droid_buffer_pool_set_config (GstBufferPool * bpool, GstStructure * config)
         (features, GST_CAPS_FEATURE_MEMORY_DROID_MEDIA_QUEUE_BUFFER);
 
     GST_DEBUG_OBJECT (pool, "Configured pool. caps: %" GST_PTR_FORMAT, caps);
-    pool->allocator = gst_droid_media_buffer_allocator_new ();
-    gst_object_ref (pool->allocator);
+    /* (the allocator of an earlier configuration stays with its memory) */
+    if (pool->allocator)
+      gst_object_unref (pool->allocator);
+    /* new, it is floating: the pool takes that reference, and frees it */
+    pool->allocator = gst_object_ref_sink (gst_droid_media_buffer_allocator_new ());
     gst_buffer_pool_config_set_allocator (config,
         (GstAllocator *) pool->allocator, &params);
     GST_OBJECT_UNLOCK (pool);
